# Direct dependencies, as version RANGES. This is the file to edit.
#
# Render and CI do not install this file. They install requirements.txt,
# which is compiled from this one and pins every package (including
# indirect ones) to an exact version, so each build gets the same code.
# Before 2026-09-25 Render installed these ranges directly with no build
# cache, so every deploy re-resolved them; on 2026-09-24 that pulled in
# SQLAlchemy 2.1 and the API crashed at boot.
#
# To add, remove or upgrade a dependency:
#   1. edit this file
#   2. cd backend && uv pip compile requirements.in --universal --python-version 3.11 -o requirements.txt
#      (add --upgrade-package NAME to move one package to its newest
#      allowed version; uv otherwise keeps the existing pins)
#   3. run the tests (cd backend && python -m pytest) and commit both files
# The first lock, 2026-09-25, pinned exactly the versions the live Render
# deploy had installed on Python 3.14.3.
fastapi>=0.115,<0.120
uvicorn[standard]>=0.30,<1
httpx>=0.27,<0.30
python-dotenv>=1.0,<2.0
pydantic>=2.11,<3
